      "problem": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{7x-4}$ for $x=7.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $7$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7x-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7\\cdot 7-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{49-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{45} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
